Register the MQA unfold filter in an FFmpeg tree.

Copy af_mqa.c and the adapter into libavfilter/ first:

    cp integration/ffmpeg/af_mqa.c ffmpeg/libavfilter/
    cp integration/common/mqa_adapter.[ch] ffmpeg/libavfilter/
    cd ffmpeg && patch -p1 < integration/ffmpeg/register.patch

then configure with the library:

    ./configure --extra-cflags=-I/path/to/mqa-decode/include \
                --extra-ldflags=-L/path/to/mqa-decode --extra-libs=-lmqadecode

configure finds the filter in allfilters.c by itself; there is nothing
else to add. Applied against FFmpeg 7.1, where it was built and run.

--- a/libavfilter/allfilters.c
+++ b/libavfilter/allfilters.c
@@
+extern const AVFilter ff_af_mqa;
 extern const AVFilter ff_af_pan;
--- a/libavfilter/Makefile
+++ b/libavfilter/Makefile
@@
+OBJS-$(CONFIG_MQA_FILTER)                    += af_mqa.o mqa_adapter.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_PAN_FILTER)                    += af_pan.o
